/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# BUG FIX: sw.js, index.html, and manifest.webmanifest must never be
# edge/browser-cached, or the browser's own byte-comparison update check
# (registration.update(), see UpdatePrompt.tsx) can be fooled into thinking
# no update exists when one actually does -- a stale cached sw.js looks
# byte-identical to what the browser last saw, so it never learns a new
# version was deployed at all, and UpdatePrompt.tsx's toast silently never
# fires (same class of bug as this whole session's tile-manifest caching
# issue, just one layer up: the vehicle for shipping fixes, not the fixes'
# own data). Cloudflare Pages' default asset-caching behavior isn't
# guaranteed to leave these three files uncached without an explicit rule
# (unlike hashed-filename JS/CSS chunks, which SHOULD be cached forever --
# left alone here on purpose, not covered by this rule).
# NOTE: Pages serves the SPA shell at "/" (and any deep link via the SPA
# fallback), never at the literal path /index.html -- a rule on /index.html
# alone matches nothing a browser actually requests. Cover the root too.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/registerSW.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
